            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"WC9GdWptxodM3rxqUu4lYwk6gDd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-PKhwdeVNMoL3vYxRYbAlk0O5gnh\">Regarding New York City as a whole, the population started at a modest 79,216 in 1800. The city experienced steady and dramatic growth throughout the period, with the population surging to 3,437,202 by 1900, representing more than a 40-fold increase in just one century. This upward trend continued into the following century, with the total population reaching 8,009,185 by 2000, marking an overall 100-fold expansion over the 200-year timeframe.</div>\n</div>",
