            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"WC9GdWptxodM3rxqUu4lYwk6gDd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\" old-record-id-GKSxdl4DDo4lZGxbCCglbIC2gjd\">Turning to the district breakdown, Manhattan dominated the city in 1800, accounting for 76% of the total population compared to just 24% for the other four districts combined. However, these proportions reversed dramatically over time. By 2000, Manhattan's share had declined substantially to only 19% of the total population, while the other districts had expanded their collective share to 81%, at 1,538,096 compared to 6,471,089, respectively.</div>\n</div>",
